<main>


<h1>
Vietnam Sourcing Project | China+1 Supply Chain Strategy Evaluation
</h1>


<h2>
Helping International Businesses Evaluate Vietnam Manufacturing Opportunities
</h2>


<p class="intro">
A sourcing project where Quick Chan supported a North American client in
evaluating Vietnam manufacturing opportunities through supplier research,
factory verification and production capability assessment.
</p>



<section>

<h2>
Project Background
</h2>


<p>
A North American client was exploring alternative manufacturing options outside
Mainland China as part of a broader China+1 supply chain diversification strategy.
</p>


<p>
The project focused on understanding Vietnam's manufacturing ecosystem,
supplier capabilities and production feasibility before making future sourcing
decisions.
</p>


</section>




<section>

<h2>
Project Scope
</h2>


<ul>

<li>
Supplier identification and Vietnam manufacturing market research
</li>

<li>
Factory verification, capability assessment and supplier qualification
</li>

<li>
Manufacturing process and production feasibility evaluation
</li>

<li>
China+1 sourcing strategy support
</li>

</ul>


</section>




<section>

<h2>
Challenge
</h2>


<p>
The key challenge was identifying suitable manufacturing partners that could
meet international buyers' expectations while accurately assessing Vietnam's
current manufacturing capabilities and limitations.
</p>


<ul>

<li>
Identifying genuine manufacturers rather than trading companies
</li>

<li>
Assessing supplier production capabilities and available equipment
</li>

<li>
Understanding material availability and manufacturing limitations
</li>

<li>
Evaluating suppliers' experience with international customers
</li>

</ul>


</section>




<section>

<h2>
Approach
</h2>


<p>
The sourcing process followed a structured supplier evaluation approach:
</p>


<ul>

<li>
Mapping potential suppliers based on product requirements, manufacturing
capabilities and production resources
</li>

<li>
Screening factories through capability evaluation and production assessment
</li>

<li>
Reviewing equipment, materials, production processes and technical capabilities
</li>

<li>
Communicating with suppliers to understand commercial feasibility and production suitability
</li>

</ul>


</section>




<section>

<h2>
Outcome
</h2>

<section>

<h2>
How HYWSource Supports Global Buyers
</h2>


<p>
HYWSource helps international companies evaluate sourcing opportunities across
Asia through supplier research, factory verification, manufacturing assessment
and procurement support.
</p>


</section>
<p>
The project provided the client with a practical assessment of Vietnam's
manufacturing landscape, including supplier capabilities, production limitations
and potential sourcing opportunities.
</p>


<p>
The findings helped the client make a more informed decision regarding China+1
sourcing strategy and potential manufacturing expansion in Vietnam.
</p>


</section>




<section>

<h2>
Key Takeaway
</h2>

<p>
Successful China+1 sourcing is not simply about finding an alternative supplier.
It requires understanding manufacturing ecosystems, evaluating supplier
capabilities and selecting partners that align with long-term business objectives.
</p>

</section>



<section>

<h2>
Professional Perspective
</h2>

<p>
Through years of procurement experience across Mainland China, Taiwan and
Vietnam, Quick Chan approaches sourcing decisions from both a buyer's perspective
and a manufacturing reality perspective.
</p>

</section>


